The standard deviation (standard error) of the sampling distribution of the sample mean under the null hypothesis is calculated as:

\[
SE = \frac{\text{sample\_std\_dev}}{\sqrt{\text{sample\_size}}}
    = \frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
    \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
    \approx 0.2213
\]

So the standard deviation of the null‑hypothesis test is **≈ 0.2213**.
